(images/82/82f400b1c1ecaa2224d27d706d714b647de00fc52289bc0979e86421102f377a.svg) | ![](images/15/156b31ede73de5301befe67f02745a0202f1806a62f9fdecc6fc9ee3f21117ba.svg) | ![](images/68/68dade17027ee6000e173cc4300792d43ded4611ea76ccd1bbbe944d0f1c33e4.svg) |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function ![](images/39/393248bc977a944f226b63d6e427db4a75fae5d9bb8223b1dd7e20dc7c6c915d.svg) given that the random variables ![](images/46/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) and ![](images/ab/ab4817775494786b06f0b9cecf225ea5979c035b69c36c1fa078f835524be9e9.svg) have the joint probability mass function ![](images/a2/a2dcac06a4cf671df0fa43cef1727449fb2ebc57fb824d19cc07da5e75d12176.svg) shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ![](images/73/73200164e7e4ed0fcd6d2b30f32e740f7a144fb66ee76bf8a22b3c39f958dfb3.svg) is defined as\n\n![](images/d0/d0b202fd64d7298dd7f1a4c4e80ae8ba1f1186ec4e90662ae45f73da799c253b.svg)\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n![](images/61/6195d748dc9306bdc6742a95785120c1db0875adc83fd07608bd023efd19be7a.svg)\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n![](images/20/2009dc5dd1ad1738cc1f50345734656e3970ab103d191929404b0ce7aa70da8f.svg)\n\nwhere ![](images/a2/a2dcac06a4cf671df0fa43cef1727449fb2ebc57fb824d19cc07da5e75d12176.svg) is the joint probability mass function of ![](images/46/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) and ![](images/07/07fd689b67975f50da1b6b025460996fc87f21f758f5e98d34eb84c9b0e50fcd.svg) and ![](images/3a/3aa9c47fc054317f2163393853c05d71714e0c9f0424297f51b46b107e222229.svg) is the marginal distribution of ![](images/02/029615e92d8b6d5c444a4daf74a9a8d63048e8d4be5f97c8207fe7af2e189e18.svg)\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for ![](images/46/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) and ![](images/ab/ab4817775494786b06f0b9cecf225ea5979c035b69c36c1fa078f835524be9e9.svg) correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| ![](images/bc/bc562d54615dad55d095db2afed7626f62ff7ebf0ab6c5d45471b77ac30b6398.svg) | ![](images/5d/5dc49d43a26a7f7c244230d64b45a8f4347c9c0c9459c2e84d09c77bab196a6a.svg) | ![](images/3b/3b30c77d4719f1a02bb918bac935a9700f7895d4a08995493dca6a9707a59888.svg) | ![](images/0d/0d08226a482630bff20558817aceb35b7ba82c3f1b1cfe5143deb07deb8726f8.svg) | ![](images/fd/fdb49440ceb7e11cd9ba0b0869a1e6d3565549969180830d1796db7dd00a2b96.svg) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ![](images/8b/8b60f9aefd30405c3034eec74ec8331ef8082ea222b7770741d259cb873f0edb.svg) | ![](images/82/82f400b1c1ecaa2224d27d706d714b647de00fc52289bc0979e86421102f377a.svg) | ![](images/15/156b31ede73de5301befe67f02745a0202f1806a62f9fdecc6fc9ee3f21117ba.svg) | ![](images/68/68dade17027ee6000e173cc4300792d43ded4611ea76ccd1bbbe944d0f1c33e4.svg) | ![](images/ae/ae6c6f895c67f3c99f98c0aa70dbcaaa6d553079bc8942a85b95d36458731a6b.svg) |\n| ![](images/74/74c80a223d4f01acbb32630508e2233df51abac691108b092579afecffa81eed.svg) | ![](images/ae/ae6c6f895c67f3c99f98c0aa70dbcaaa6d553079bc8942a85b95d36458731a6b.svg) | ![](images/82/82f400b1c1ecaa2224d27d706d714b647de00fc52289bc0979e86421102f377a.svg) | ![](images/15/156b31ede73de5301befe67f02745a0202f1806a62f9fdecc6fc9ee3f21117ba.svg) | ![](images/43/43dec3bb0f167a8fc4d34f800d49bcc041c36b6da8c5df0ab6eff97d1804d5c6.svg) |\n| ![](images/2a/2af6da210d7b2077279622a81cd96521db7accd90fa91c8f1a467c7c0ea63ecc.svg) | ![](images/82/82f400b1c1ecaa2224d27d706d714b647de00fc52289bc0979e86421102f377a.svg) | ![](images/15/156b31ede73de5301befe67f02745a0202f1806a62f9fdecc6fc9ee3f21117ba.svg) | ![](images/68/68dade17027ee6000e173cc4300792d43ded4611ea76ccd1bbbe944d0f1c33e4.svg) | ![](images/ae/ae6c6f895c67f3c99f98c0aa70dbcaaa6d553079bc8942a85b95d36458731a6b.svg) |\n| ![](images/3a/3aa9c47fc054317f2163393853c05d71714e0c9f0424297f51b46b107e222229.svg) | ![](images/0b/0b47cf9f83219ef6bab2ac82c70ded537ce9db2ab3945b85d5ca678f16b30a75.svg) | ![](images/ae/ae6c6f895c67f3c99f98c0aa70dbcaaa6d553079bc8942a85b95d36458731a6b.svg) | ![](images/68/68dade17027ee6000e173cc4300792d43ded4611ea76ccd1bbbe944d0f1c33e4.svg) | ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) |\n\nTherefore, for ![](images/02/027b707633da7c0c044a94992bbc3e3af329c5637a1d359c2a7dc8d7f87adf64.svg) we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/df/df523a1ccd89260e6b6d9d722b5339bf045050e30100c86c75dff65a75d192a6.svg)\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) | ![](images/15/156b31ede73de5301befe67f02745a0202f1806a62f9fdecc6fc9ee3f21117ba.svg) | ![](images/f5/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) | ![](images/40/402ff5d0c0c3aaa47f18c89f6d96c95d47840eac13822d596a51bdb0c5f9a4ab.svg) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ![](images/39/393248bc977a944f226b63d6e427db4a75fae5d9bb8223b1dd7e20dc7c6c915d.svg) | ![](images/93/93e08787a61d8cca64eb3502ac419eb60504d75ad064927243c22a315430ab3e.svg) | ![](images/16/1627bb3010ada55ed941966d38081f1a6c1394c07ca78b94585f8c97e4bbc138.svg) | ![](images/93/93e08787a61d8cca64eb3502ac419eb60504d75ad064927243c22a315430ab3e.svg) |" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162372 :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P(Y=3\\,|\\,X=2)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required probability is given by\n\n$$\nP(Y=3\\,|\\,X=2)=\\frac{P(X=2,Y=3)}{P(X=2)}=\\frac{f(2,3)}{{f}_{X}(2)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(2) & =0.05+0.25 \\\\  & =0.30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(2,3)=0.25.$ \n\nFinally, substituting ${f}_{X}(2)=0.30$ and $f(2,3)=0.25$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=3\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{f(2,3)}{{f}_{X}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.25}{0.30} \\\\  & ≈0.83.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159434 :answer-field/correct 17592186159436 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-dd1f8e38-c35e-55be-bdf0-b84dac107dde" :question/id #uuid "dd1f8e38-c35e-55be-bdf0-b84dac107dde" :question/math-academy-id "q-142884" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ |\n\nCompute $P(Y=0\\,|\\,X=3)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required probability is given by\n\n$$\nP(Y=0\\,|\\,X=3)=\\frac{P(X=3,Y=0)}{P(X=3)}=\\frac{f(3,0)}{{f}_{X}(3)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(3) & =f(3,0)+f(3,1)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{18}+\\frac{2}{18}+\\frac{1}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(3,0)=\\frac{1}{9}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting ${f}_{X}(3)=\\frac{5}{18}$ and $f(3,0)=\\frac{1}{9}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=0\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{f(3,0)}{{f}_{X}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{9})}{(\\frac{5}{18})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-267ccec5-8a84-5cdf-a568-00ac33d5a7c7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-267ccec5-8a84-5cdf-a568-00ac33d5a7c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "267ccec5-8a84-5cdf-a568-00ac33d5a7c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f9b91a68-f1a7-5800-9852-2b8c8adc0a07" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7df7cc62-41f2-5b67-8003-b3f2f792fe42" "answer-dd26a283-a544-5be7-b680-07b8f95e6c0e" "answer-cece1cdf-fe31-5b7b-9e6c-984391d3198f" "answer-9258e615-4af2-514e-a284-343d0ce33226" "answer-f9b91a68-f1a7-5800-9852-2b8c8adc0a07"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7df7cc62-41f2-5b67-8003-b3f2f792fe42" :answer/id #uuid "7df7cc62-41f2-5b67-8003-b3f2f792fe42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd26a283-a544-5be7-b680-07b8f95e6c0e" :answer/id #uuid "dd26a283-a544-5be7-b680-07b8f95e6c0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cece1cdf-fe31-5b7b-9e6c-984391d3198f" :answer/id #uuid "cece1cdf-fe31-5b7b-9e6c-984391d3198f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9258e615-4af2-514e-a284-343d0ce33226" :answer/id #uuid "9258e615-4af2-514e-a284-343d0ce33226" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9b91a68-f1a7-5800-9852-2b8c8adc0a07" :answer/id #uuid "f9b91a68-f1a7-5800-9852-2b8c8adc0a07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5f05ade6-f4a6-518d-b188-3b387ae00a2d" :question/id #uuid "5f05ade6-f4a6-518d-b188-3b387ae00a2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142862" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n\nCompute $P(1<Y<7\\,|\\,X=2)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<Y<7\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{P((1<Y<7),X=2)}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=2,(1<Y<7))}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=2,Y=3)+P(X=2,Y=5)}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2,3)+f(2,5)}{{f}_{X}(2)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(2) & =f(2,1)+f(2,3)+f(2,5)+f(2,7) \\\\  & =0+0.05+0.05+0.1 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(2,3)=0.05$ and $f(2,5)=0.05.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<Y<7\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{f(2,3)+f(2,5)}{{f}_{X}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.05+0.05}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1}{0.2} \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28ba60db-712f-5d88-8bab-1c42ece049bb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28ba60db-712f-5d88-8bab-1c42ece049bb" :answer-field/id #uuid "28ba60db-712f-5d88-8bab-1c42ece049bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cfc7ea99-dc34-5c5e-b665-c3586432a818" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5da297a0-8c40-5743-92dd-89674c59b084" "answer-778478e6-34f7-5241-9c21-a6104ba3033d" "answer-558ce6b2-7ed9-580c-a0dc-2f742abaac0a" "answer-cfc7ea99-dc34-5c5e-b665-c3586432a818" "answer-b8532e0e-af6a-5a33-b916-4185a356c949"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5da297a0-8c40-5743-92dd-89674c59b084" :answer/id #uuid "5da297a0-8c40-5743-92dd-89674c59b084" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-778478e6-34f7-5241-9c21-a6104ba3033d" :answer/id #uuid "778478e6-34f7-5241-9c21-a6104ba3033d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-558ce6b2-7ed9-580c-a0dc-2f742abaac0a" :answer/id #uuid "558ce6b2-7ed9-580c-a0dc-2f742abaac0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfc7ea99-dc34-5c5e-b665-c3586432a818" :answer/id #uuid "cfc7ea99-dc34-5c5e-b665-c3586432a818" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8532e0e-af6a-5a33-b916-4185a356c949" :answer/id #uuid "b8532e0e-af6a-5a33-b916-4185a356c949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-29c9824b-2b87-54bb-a940-69ce3efe0d1b" :question/id #uuid "29c9824b-2b87-54bb-a940-69ce3efe0d1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-142904" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n\nCompute $P(0\\le X<2\\,|\\,Y=4)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X<2\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{P((0\\le X<2),Y=4)}{P(Y=4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=0,Y=4)+P(X=1,Y=4)}{P(Y=4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0,4)+f(1,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(4) & =f(0,4)+f(1,4)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.1+0.05 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(0,4)=0.05$ and $f(1,4)=0.1.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X<2\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(0,4)+f(1,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.05+0.1}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.15}{0.2} \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-78621176-1e00-508c-804a-571ad3daf5d2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-78621176-1e00-508c-804a-571ad3daf5d2" :answer-field/id #uuid "78621176-1e00-508c-804a-571ad3daf5d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-10a5a9d4-3a44-5769-9f6b-52e2cb75f730" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4a0b152-342f-53f4-afe1-60a1eb558763" "answer-bb32d8a6-9c26-5a27-9faa-26691c347856" "answer-4bcd313c-8a81-5a91-877f-2970fdc8ac87" "answer-2f47c227-7ea9-5c71-8c0a-c370a8c2740e" "answer-10a5a9d4-3a44-5769-9f6b-52e2cb75f730"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4a0b152-342f-53f4-afe1-60a1eb558763" :answer/id #uuid "c4a0b152-342f-53f4-afe1-60a1eb558763" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb32d8a6-9c26-5a27-9faa-26691c347856" :answer/id #uuid "bb32d8a6-9c26-5a27-9faa-26691c347856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bcd313c-8a81-5a91-877f-2970fdc8ac87" :answer/id #uuid "4bcd313c-8a81-5a91-877f-2970fdc8ac87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f47c227-7ea9-5c71-8c0a-c370a8c2740e" :answer/id #uuid "2f47c227-7ea9-5c71-8c0a-c370a8c2740e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10a5a9d4-3a44-5769-9f6b-52e2cb75f730" :answer/id #uuid "10a5a9d4-3a44-5769-9f6b-52e2cb75f730" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4ab049c7-8771-5b28-bd3b-011a826d75ca" :question/id #uuid "4ab049c7-8771-5b28-bd3b-011a826d75ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-142936" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=2)\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=x\\,|\\,Y=2)=\\frac{P(X=x,Y=2)}{P(Y=2)}=\\frac{f(x,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for $X$ and $Y$ correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $x\\in \\{0,2,4\\},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(0,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.4}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=2\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(2,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)}=\\frac{0.2}{0.4}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(X=4\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(4,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.4}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-295a6c8e-d0f1-5ddc-b043-2d9d231b86a4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-295a6c8e-d0f1-5ddc-b043-2d9d231b86a4" :answer-field/id #uuid "295a6c8e-d0f1-5ddc-b043-2d9d231b86a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b4efca0f-c1ba-5117-b9f7-7813f9a55b58" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06f6b37e-e1c4-56fe-af0d-d05220252493" "answer-b4efca0f-c1ba-5117-b9f7-7813f9a55b58" "answer-b80e5bda-3113-58c2-972b-15fe4ed4a1f9" "answer-4329cac3-a508-561d-92e3-75791b4b2a53" "answer-6429f8f1-6f22-5c87-b7fa-2aa976d2cf28"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06f6b37e-e1c4-56fe-af0d-d05220252493" :answer/id #uuid "06f6b37e-e1c4-56fe-af0d-d05220252493" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4efca0f-c1ba-5117-b9f7-7813f9a55b58" :answer/id #uuid "b4efca0f-c1ba-5117-b9f7-7813f9a55b58" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b80e5bda-3113-58c2-972b-15fe4ed4a1f9" :answer/id #uuid "b80e5bda-3113-58c2-972b-15fe4ed4a1f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4329cac3-a508-561d-92e3-75791b4b2a53" :answer/id #uuid "4329cac3-a508-561d-92e3-75791b4b2a53" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6429f8f1-6f22-5c87-b7fa-2aa976d2cf28" :answer/id #uuid "6429f8f1-6f22-5c87-b7fa-2aa976d2cf28" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162374 :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=2)\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=y\\,|\\,X=2)=\\frac{P(X=2,Y=y)}{P(X=2)}=\\frac{f(2,y)}{{f}_{X}(2)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for $X$ and $Y$ correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $y\\in \\{0,1,2\\},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=0\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{f(2,0)}{{f}_{X}(2)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.6}=\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(Y=1\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{f(2,1)}{{f}_{X}(2)}=\\frac{0.2}{0.6}=\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ P(Y=2\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{f(2,2)}{{f}_{X}(2)}=\\frac{0.3}{0.6}=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159446 :answer-field/correct "answer-9439ac72-3a37-5eb2-990d-61250e8eb639" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c2c0f42e-45c2-566f-9ec2-8be256c299d9" "answer-02d64482-a157-593b-a0d1-db5b6744fac2" "answer-fbdc667d-fd73-5bf1-b510-9e033c858f0c" "answer-9439ac72-3a37-5eb2-990d-61250e8eb639" "answer-33614170-1060-5986-98ed-e0d47798ec54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2c0f42e-45c2-566f-9ec2-8be256c299d9" :answer/id #uuid "c2c0f42e-45c2-566f-9ec2-8be256c299d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02d64482-a157-593b-a0d1-db5b6744fac2" :answer/id #uuid "02d64482-a157-593b-a0d1-db5b6744fac2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbdc667d-fd73-5bf1-b510-9e033c858f0c" :answer/id #uuid "fbdc667d-fd73-5bf1-b510-9e033c858f0c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9439ac72-3a37-5eb2-990d-61250e8eb639" :answer/id #uuid "9439ac72-3a37-5eb2-990d-61250e8eb639" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33614170-1060-5986-98ed-e0d47798ec54" :answer/id #uuid "33614170-1060-5986-98ed-e0d47798ec54" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163288 :tutorial/content "Let's recall the multiplication law for conditional probability for two events ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) and ![](images/5d/5d8b650b90c85fbc0db5e4b6fae61767e293a843d18a2526f3ee4157733e1f4b.svg)\n![](images/44/44229a2a35108e36c1348009a552be50e798af9b2807f49c4e4ef8515ed7eefe.svg)\n\nNow suppose that ![](images/46/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) and ![](images/ab/ab4817775494786b06f0b9cecf225ea5979c035b69c36c1fa078f835524be9e9.svg) are discrete random variables. The conditional probability that ![](images/2c/2cc57b1c8b00862c078193ea1774f4012e1513ab1a26a6d5bb806e046220a812.svg) *given that* ![](images/46/46851627a248368806191a89ed2bb59d72b83b2e352f768da26f41305e156052.svg) follows immediately from the multiplication law and is given by\n\n![](images/2b/2b705d0acedbb080625148287647d075dce75f40531615a52352a848a85892fe.svg)\n\nwhere ![](images/a2/a2dcac06a4cf671df0fa43cef1727449fb2ebc57fb824d19cc07da5e75d12176.svg) is the joint PMF of ![](images/46/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) and ![](images/07/07fd689b67975f50da1b6b025460996fc87f21f758f5e98d34eb84c9b0e50fcd.svg) and ![](images/3a/3aa9c47fc054317f2163393853c05d71714e0c9f0424297f51b46b107e222229.svg) is the marginal mass function of ![](images/02/029615e92d8b6d5c444a4daf74a9a8d63048e8d4be5f97c8207fe7af2e189e18.svg)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- To avoid getting a zero in the denominator, this formula assumes that ![](images/f4/f40e8e149f4e148b5042516dae366a5d17bdc00e1d6e39e27ddf30ece6801d6f.svg)\n\n- If ![](images/0f/0fa3deb4b6345d48bdeeb06c02ecd3d9bcf6a68cf517412b251a2bcf1e67d07f.svg) then ![](images/ad/ad17cd2272c82a9380977e2ef9ff99fb613681da7df20c06949db320c701bc4c.svg) is not defined by the usual conditional probability formula, since the denominator is zero. In this discrete setting, we therefore restrict the formula to values of ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) for which ![](images/1e/1ebc42b48118a4c62d7203d91e76ecc1a865f8d536cf145c82499ac8fd531cc7.svg)\n\nIn a similar manner, the conditional probability that ![](images/46/46851627a248368806191a89ed2bb59d72b83b2e352f768da26f41305e156052.svg) given that ![](images/2c/2cc57b1c8b00862c078193ea1774f4012e1513ab1a26a6d5bb806e046220a812.svg) can be calculated as\n![](images/8c/8c8bdddcd02a672d59ded44b5281cf2f24236f88b2f494730bac998a760e9b0a.svg)\n\nwhere ![](images/fd/fdb49440ceb7e11cd9ba0b0869a1e6d3565549969180830d1796db7dd00a2b96.svg) is the marginal mass function of ![](images/ed/ed6dc1fd057e3dd2207c735a562bf4db22b72d1a9380651607439f00c0440725.svg) This formula assumes that ![](images/f8/f8020df80e303daf760cd9bf4d8437cc08bc4b95b0ccf64bc7a43ccddc650f5f.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163325 :tutorial/content "We can now define two more probability mass functions as follows:\n\n- The **conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$,** denoted $f_{X|Y}(x|y),$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf_{X|Y}(x|y) = P(X = x \\,|\\, Y = y) = \\dfrac{P(X = x, \\, Y = y)}{P(Y=y)} = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_Y(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere  $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and $f_Y(y)$ is the marginal mass function of $Y.$\n\n- The **conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x,$** denoted $f_{Y|X}(y|x),$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf_{Y|X}(y|x) = P(Y = y \\,|\\, X = x) = \\dfrac{P(X = x,\\, Y = y)}{P(X=x)} = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_X(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere  $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and $f_X(x)$ is the marginal mass function of $X.$\n\n**Watch out!** The conditional distribution of $X$ given $Y$ does *not* equal the conditional distribution of $Y$ given $X$. That is, in general,\n\n$$\nf_{X|Y}(x|y)  \\ne f_{Y|X}(y|x).\n$$\n\nFinally, if $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then \n\n$$\nf_{X|Y}(x|y)=f_X(x),\\qquad f_{Y|X}(y|x)=f_Y(y).\n$$\n\nIn other words, if $X$  and  $Y$ are independent, then knowing the value of one random variable does not affect the probability distribution of the other." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162164 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
